SteamARM: X windows with a layer in Mission Control

Mission Control lays the overlay NSWindows (remoteLayerCocoa.m) out as
windows of their own, with the game's picture, but leaves the Xplugin
frames where they are: the window server does not hand them to it. Under a
layer a frame's pixels are the X window's background, so a white window
stood in the middle of Mission Control, at the X window's place; and a
window whose whole area is a descendant's layer -- steamwebhelper's
toplevel, under the GPU process's child with the picture -- showed as an
empty window beside it (the user's screenshots, 2026-10-04).

While Mission Control is open -- WindowManager's shield window, at the
utility level and a display's size, is on screen; checked every 100 ms
while an overlay is, the window descriptions read only when the windows on
screen change -- the frames under layers are made transparent
(SLSSetWindowAlpha) and the covered overlays (XQRemoteLayerState.covered,
xprRemoteLayer.c) ordered out; both come back when it closes (a covered
overlay once its frame is on screen again, so one closed on another Space
stays with it). Ordering the overlay into its frame's window-server group,
or making it transient, did not change what Mission Control showed
(measured with the user). XQUARTZ_RL_MISSION_CONTROL=0 leaves it as
before.
